    {
      "text": "should not people seek unto their God for living to hear from dead, 2 Ne. 18:19. law hath become dead unto us, 2 Ne. 25:25. by knowing deadness of law, men may look forward to that life which is in Christ, 2 Ne. 25:27. words of faithful shall speak as if it were from dead, 2 Ne. 27:13 (Morm. 8:26; 9:30; Moro. 10:27). baptism covenant to serve God until dead as to mortal body, Mosiah 18:13. he that becomes child of devil is dead unto all good works, Alma 5:41–42. Lamoni lies as though dead for two days and nights, Alma 18:43; 19:1–8, 18. Korihor claims that when man is dead, that is end, Alma 30:18. all mankind, being cut off from presence of the Lord by Fall of Adam, are considered as dead, Hel. 14:16. it is mockery before God, putting trust in dead works, Moro. 8:23. Jehovah, the Eternal Judge of both quick and dead, Moro. 10:34.",
